  "source": "The Swedish Council for Information on Alcohol and Other Drugs (CAN)",
  "note": [
    "Indicator definition: Percentage (%) of pupils in school year 9 and year 2 of upper secondary school that have consumed alcohol over the past 12 months and purchased alcoholic beverages on the Internet. Questions: 'Have you ever drank alcohol (do not include drinks below 2.26 %, for example, low-alcohol beer or weak cider)?' and 'Have you purchased alcohol on the Internet over the past 12 months?' The indicator refers to the percentage that replied 'Yes, over the past 30 days' and/or 'Yes, over the past 12 months' and for the second question 'Yes, 1-2 times' or 'Yes, 3 times or more'."
  ]
